//@ typecheck-fail
//@ requires: madaros
//@ error-pattern: E221
// `atan` and four siblings are bound for typechecking and absent from the
// backend, so the call used to compile to an ELF and die on an illegal
// instruction. Measured before this refusal: `print_f64(atan(0.5))` alone gave
// check rc=0, compile rc=0, run rc=132 -- and the same for tan, tanh, asin and
// acos. sin, cos, exp, log and sqrt have builtin ids and are unaffected.
//
// requires: madaros is load-bearing. CI's suite compiles with souc-stage2,
// built from self-hosted/compiler/lean_single.sio, which implements all five
// and must not be asked to refuse them.

fn main() with IO, Mut, Div {
    print_f64(atan(0.5))
    print("\n")
}
